WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.139 --> 00:00:05.450
Hey youtubers it’s Charlie hopefully you
guys have all had a chance to re-watch the

00:00:05.450 --> 00:00:06.720
doctor who premiere a few times.

00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:10.620
In my review I asked you to submit questions
so we’ll try to answer some of the big ones.

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:14.230
I think the biggest types of questions were
Missy related and the the big changes.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:16.580
There are a few important things that I’m
going to mention after all the question but

00:00:16.580 --> 00:00:18.230
let’s talk about the episode first.

00:00:18.230 --> 00:00:20.840
Careful for spoilers if you haven’t seen
it yet.

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.060
I’ll wait just a sec...okay, here we go

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:30.050
Question 1 - amazedsatsuma asks Could Missy
be Mercy Hartigan from The Next Doctor Special?

00:00:30.050 --> 00:00:34.989
There were so many Missy theories that I’ll
see if I can sum them all up in this one question,

00:00:34.989 --> 00:00:37.510
so this will go on a little bit longer than
the other questions.

00:00:37.510 --> 00:00:39.399
There are a few things we know about the finale.

00:00:39.399 --> 00:00:42.930
It involves Missy and the Cybermen and Heaven.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.850
The title of the final episode is Death in
Heaven.

00:00:45.850 --> 00:00:47.989
There were a lot of suggestions you guys all
had in the comments.

00:00:47.989 --> 00:00:53.300
Mercy was one of them, as was Susan Foreman
the Doctor’s Granddaughter, Romana, The

00:00:53.300 --> 00:00:58.449
Rani, Tasha Lem, A Female Master or Mistress
I guess you’d call her, because she’s

00:00:58.449 --> 00:00:59.449
a woman.

00:00:59.449 --> 00:01:03.230
And another personification of the TARDIS,
like in The Doctor’s Wife episode.

00:01:03.230 --> 00:01:07.409
Some of you guys actually wrote some really
well thought out theories.

00:01:07.409 --> 00:01:10.520
Right now my favorites are Susan Foreman and
a female Master.

00:01:10.520 --> 00:01:14.030
Another commenter Zachary had a really good
explanation for the Susan theory.

00:01:14.030 --> 00:01:17.360
First, the doctor left her in the far future
and promised to come back.

00:01:17.360 --> 00:01:18.750
But he never did.

00:01:18.750 --> 00:01:22.020
Remember how I said the Doctor leaving people
behind was a recurring theme in Deep Breath.

00:01:22.020 --> 00:01:24.920
As well as The Girl who Waited.

00:01:24.920 --> 00:01:30.890
It’s possible that Missy is a future version
of Susan, but it requires that some rules

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:34.090
get bent on the resort planet from that Amy
Pond episode.

00:01:34.090 --> 00:01:38.200
The disease there killed people with two hearts,
so Susan would technically die if Paradise

00:01:38.200 --> 00:01:39.250
was that same planet.

00:01:39.250 --> 00:01:43.560
I don’t think that’s the case, I think
Missy is in a pocket universe.

00:01:43.560 --> 00:01:44.560
The Nethersphere.

00:01:44.560 --> 00:01:49.659
I think she’s called the gatekeeper just
because she controls access.

00:01:49.659 --> 00:02:00.680
If you look at Moffat’s quote about the
finale too, remember the doctor made a promise

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:01.869
to susan.

00:02:01.869 --> 00:02:04.070
The synopsis reads.

00:02:04.070 --> 00:02:05.670
"You betrayed me.

00:02:05.670 --> 00:02:10.380
You betrayed my trust, our friendship, and
everything I've ever stood for.

00:02:10.380 --> 00:02:11.380
You let me down."

00:02:11.380 --> 00:02:21.770
- that could be a lot of people saying that
though.

00:02:21.770 --> 00:02:24.319
The next best theory is Rani.

00:02:24.319 --> 00:02:28.950
I don’t remember, but she might have been
stuck in a pocket universe at some point.

00:02:28.950 --> 00:02:35.340
She did have a lot of stories involving dinosaurs.

00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:38.319
Supposedly in the novels she had her head
cut off though.

00:02:38.319 --> 00:02:45.790
Plus, I don’t think the Rani ever had the
sexualized obsession with the doctor Missy

00:02:45.790 --> 00:02:46.850
seems to have.

00:02:46.850 --> 00:02:48.300
Then there’s The Female Master.

00:02:48.300 --> 00:02:50.659
Mistress is certainly a play on that.

00:02:50.659 --> 00:02:56.910
And you could say that the doctor and the
master have shared a very co-dependent relationship.

00:02:56.910 --> 00:03:00.610
Moffat said that The Master was dead and gone,
but it could be a Moffat lies situation where

00:03:00.610 --> 00:03:03.120
yes, the Master is gone, but only because
he’s The Mistress now.

00:03:03.120 --> 00:03:04.810
Viewing that as a different character.

00:03:04.810 --> 00:03:11.239
Then there’s Tasha Lem, who could have found
a way to change herself to fix the Dalek assimilation.

00:03:11.239 --> 00:03:13.940
She and the Doctor had a sexual relationship
at one point.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:19.080
But the vibe I got from Missy was so sinister
that I don’t think it was Tasha.

00:03:19.080 --> 00:03:27.511
The 
TARDIS theories all stem from the use of the

00:03:27.511 --> 00:03:33.960
word Sexy, like Missy could be some of the
essence of The TARDIS in female form.

00:03:33.960 --> 00:03:37.700
She also refers to the Doctor’s new accent
and says “I’ll keep it”.

00:03:37.700 --> 00:03:47.980
Remember that the TARDIS said she originally
stole the Doctor, the Doctor didn’t steal

00:03:47.980 --> 00:03:48.980
her.

00:03:48.980 --> 00:03:52.260
On top of all that, if you look at the brooches
both Clara and Missy were wearing.

00:03:52.260 --> 00:03:58.070
Clara’s looked like the untempered schism
and Missy’s reminded me of the Lady in White.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:00.959
So I guess you could add Lady in White to
the list of possibilities.

00:04:00.959 --> 00:04:03.250
Although she seems more like the Doctor’s
mother.

00:04:03.250 --> 00:04:04.860
Not his girlfriend.

00:04:04.860 --> 00:04:10.720
So best three theories right now are Susan,
TARDIS Essence and The Mistress.

00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:15.390
Question 2 - Vicram Films asks Did you notice
that he told the robot that you have changed

00:04:15.390 --> 00:04:18.550
your parts so many times, that there is no
trace of you left?

00:04:18.550 --> 00:04:19.550
Was that also a reference to himself?

00:04:19.550 --> 00:04:23.700
He has changed so many times that there is
no trace of his original self left?

00:04:23.700 --> 00:04:28.080
Good question, yes he was totally talking
to himself as much as the Robot.

00:04:28.080 --> 00:04:31.522
Moffat said a long time ago that the Doctor
would regenerate past his limit but that there

00:04:31.522 --> 00:04:32.950
would be consequences.

00:04:32.950 --> 00:04:38.310
Now we know that the Time Lords gave him a
new cycle, which harkens back to Deadly Assassin,

00:04:38.310 --> 00:04:41.450
when the Master tried to steal a new cycle.

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:46.410
I think there are still original aspects of
his first self inside there.

00:04:46.410 --> 00:04:49.270
I think it just takes him longer to find them
in his mind palace.

00:04:49.270 --> 00:04:50.370
He keeps having trouble remembering things.

00:04:50.370 --> 00:04:52.570
I think that as he continues to regenerate
it will get worse.

00:04:52.570 --> 00:04:56.050
That whole exchange is seeding a big plot
for series 8.

00:04:56.050 --> 00:04:59.660
The doctor remembering his face and correcting
mistakes of the past will be big recurring

00:04:59.660 --> 00:05:01.330
themes.

00:05:01.330 --> 00:05:06.630
Question 3 - James Swift do you think that
the fires of Pompeii Capaldi is The Doctor

00:05:06.630 --> 00:05:08.980
in human form using the pocket watch?

00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:10.430
Good Pocketwatch question.

00:05:10.430 --> 00:05:11.740
No I don’t think so.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:18.210
I think some of his familiar face talk was
acknowledging the meta thing happening.

00:05:18.210 --> 00:05:21.310
But I don’t think fires of pompeii capaldi
will go further than that.

00:05:21.310 --> 00:05:23.630
I don’t think it’s some big major thing.

00:05:23.630 --> 00:05:27.980
I think someone else in the comments pointed
out that Colin Baker guest starred on Doctor

00:05:27.980 --> 00:05:29.290
Who before becoming the Doctor.

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:32.640
So it’s happened before.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:38.200
Koglin JV actually pointed out that the 'tramp'
the doctor supposedly gave the watch to is

00:05:38.200 --> 00:05:43.090
actually Elizabeth Sladen's real life husband.

00:05:43.090 --> 00:05:47.950
Question 4 - Nayef asks Hey charlie, does
the doctor choice, how he look when regenerate

00:05:47.950 --> 00:05:49.630
or same else,choice for him.

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:52.370
The Doctor can influence regenerations under
certain conditions.

00:05:52.370 --> 00:05:58.990
The Master is the only Time Lord that has
complete control over his appearance regardless

00:05:58.990 --> 00:06:00.250
of circumstance.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:03.870
The Sisterhood of the Karn have an elixir
that can control regenerations.

00:06:03.870 --> 00:06:09.000
During The Night of the Doctor Paul McGann
regenerates into John Hurt specifically choosing

00:06:09.000 --> 00:06:11.080
to become more of a warrior.

00:06:11.080 --> 00:06:23.000
Usually it’s just a measure of skill, but
there’s still a degree of chance involved.

00:06:23.000 --> 00:06:26.280
It’s possible for a forced regeneration
to result in disfigurement.

00:06:26.280 --> 00:06:29.221
But I think they only get into that in the
novels.

00:06:29.221 --> 00:06:33.100
As the series has gone on, the producers have
added layers of complexity to the science

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:34.100
of regeneration.

00:06:34.100 --> 00:06:38.270
So presumably Moffat will explain what some
of the consequences of going beyond 12 are.

00:06:38.270 --> 00:06:43.870
There’s a really old explanation that Rassilon
imposed the rule of 12 for a specific reason

00:06:43.870 --> 00:06:47.720
but I couldn’t find a satisfactory answer
other than it wasn’t punitive.

00:06:47.720 --> 00:06:51.500
He wasn’t punishing the Time Lords by imposing
the limit of 12.

00:06:51.500 --> 00:06:55.150
Question 5 - Shelley Summers asks What’s
the big deal with the Doctor giving the man

00:06:55.150 --> 00:06:57.340
his watch?

00:06:57.340 --> 00:07:03.560
The doctor can store his time lord essence
in it.

00:07:03.560 --> 00:07:05.770
All his memories and his regenerations.

00:07:05.770 --> 00:07:09.400
They’re using the pocketwatch titles now,
so I don’t know if that’s going to tie

00:07:09.400 --> 00:07:13.590
in with the Doctor’s actual pocketwatch
or if it’s just a coincidence.

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:15.780
Not everything that Moffat does is about foreshadowing.

00:07:15.780 --> 00:07:19.050
Originally when he wrote River Song into the
series during David Tennant’s run, he didn’t

00:07:19.050 --> 00:07:23.070
know that he’d use her as Amy and Rory’s
daughter when he took over the series.

00:07:23.070 --> 00:07:24.070
And the Master’s pocketwatch was something
Russell Davies did.

00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:25.070
I don’t know that they’d do something
similar so soon.

00:07:25.070 --> 00:07:28.560
But the watch itself is just an infamous piece
of Time Lord technology.

00:07:28.560 --> 00:07:32.830
Question 6- Sushant mentions what about the
Doctor’s Ring that we got a good look at

00:07:32.830 --> 00:07:33.830
after the phonecall

00:07:33.830 --> 00:07:37.120
Okay, thank you for mentioning this, I forgot
to include it in my review.

00:07:37.120 --> 00:07:54.050
The Ring is going to be part of the story
in Series 8.

00:07:54.050 --> 00:07:58.340
The first Doctor wore a blue signet ring that
had some special abilities.

00:07:58.340 --> 00:08:02.130
The Seventh Doctor later found it and started
wearing it again.

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:05.300
It also belonged to The Other at one point.

00:08:05.300 --> 00:08:08.570
The Other was one of the founders of the Time
Lord’s Society along with Rassilon and Omega.

00:08:08.570 --> 00:08:14.450
There was a bit of an easter egg during the
episode where the Robot Leader asks Clara

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:15.770
where the “Other” is.

00:08:15.770 --> 00:08:20.010
He never calls Capaldi the Doctor, he calls
him “The Other”.

00:08:20.010 --> 00:08:29.340
Supposedly, The Other tried to escape Gallifrey
when Rassilon started to consolidate his power.

00:08:29.340 --> 00:08:33.590
He entered the Looms, which were the devices
the Time Lords used to procreate.

00:08:33.590 --> 00:08:38.270
The Looms weaved genetic material together
to create new children.

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:40.382
Further rumors, The Other was reconstituted
10 Million years later as the First Doctor.

00:08:40.382 --> 00:08:43.640
That story was from the novels.

00:08:43.640 --> 00:08:45.580
Not the regular series.

00:08:45.580 --> 00:08:48.940
I guess you can take the validity of that
claim based on how much you think the novels

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:49.940
are canon.

00:08:49.940 --> 00:08:52.800
That doesn’t mean The Doctor is secretly
The Other, I think it’s just the writers

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:53.800
winking at us.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:54.800
If they included a joke about the Scottish
referendum, than you can bet there are plenty

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.620
of more obscure references throughout.

00:08:56.620 --> 00:09:00.800
Some of them are visual, like the Brooches
Missy and Clara wore and some are verbal.

00:09:00.800 --> 00:09:05.380
Question 7 - ApolloNik asks What do you think
the writing in chalk all over the bedroom

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:06.540
was all about?

00:09:06.540 --> 00:09:09.890
I think that’s Capaldi’s cracks in the
universe.

00:09:09.890 --> 00:09:12.470
I think that he will find gallifrey at some
point this series.

00:09:12.470 --> 00:09:13.820
It’s currently in a pocket universe.

00:09:13.820 --> 00:09:16.910
And the equations will have something to do
with getting there.

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:20.360
I also think they’ll tie in with the Missy
plot and the Nethersphere.

00:09:20.360 --> 00:09:25.430
I also think the Nethersphere has something
to do with the pocket universe.

00:09:25.430 --> 00:09:30.260
and Question 8 - Louie asks now Capaldi is
an older doctor will he start to get slightly

00:09:30.260 --> 00:09:31.710
older companions?

00:09:31.710 --> 00:09:35.090
or will we start to see old enemies such as
the zygons return?

00:09:35.090 --> 00:09:38.870
They did say revisiting old faces.

00:09:38.870 --> 00:09:44.570
And the synopsis for the finale says that
old enemies return.

00:09:44.570 --> 00:09:47.590
As to which old faces are returning I have
no idea.

00:09:47.590 --> 00:09:49.220
But you can reference my favorite Missy theories.

00:09:49.220 --> 00:09:51.330
We did see all the cybermen pictures.

00:09:51.330 --> 00:09:53.150
And the Daleks are back.

00:09:53.150 --> 00:09:55.970
Like the doctor said in the episode, I’ve
seen this before.

00:09:55.970 --> 00:10:00.790
My hope is that they use all these familiar
things in new and interesting ways.

00:10:00.790 --> 00:10:11.860
But everybody will have their own opinion
on that.

00:10:11.860 --> 00:10:14.220
Thanks so much for submitting questions everyone.

00:10:14.220 --> 00:10:18.060
It’s going to be a lot of fun talking about
doctor who with you guys this series.

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:22.800
I’ll always wait a day after posting review
to post Q&amp;As just to give people time to watch

00:10:22.800 --> 00:10:23.800
the episode.

00:10:23.800 --> 00:10:26.340
And Congratulations to the winners of this
week’s giveaway.

00:10:26.340 --> 00:10:28.880
smalley mcsmall &amp; Rosie Howe.

00:10:28.880 --> 00:10:35.140
Usually there’s just one weekly winner but
I’m so happy Doctor Who is back I’m doubling

00:10:35.140 --> 00:10:36.140
it.

00:10:36.140 --> 00:10:37.140
You guys both win amazon gift cards.

00:10:37.140 --> 00:10:38.760
I’ll message you on your channels for details.

00:10:38.760 --> 00:10:42.550
I also wanted to thank everyone for being
so polite in the comments.

00:10:42.550 --> 00:10:48.761
I knew there would be a lot of extreme opinions
because of all the big changes but all of

00:10:48.761 --> 00:10:53.630
you did a great job of explaining why you
didn’t like things without personally attacking

00:10:53.630 --> 00:10:54.630
moffat.

00:10:54.630 --> 00:10:58.570
There was a really awesome gif I posted that
summed up a lot of feelings in a really simple

00:10:58.570 --> 00:10:59.570
way.

00:10:59.570 --> 00:11:01.450
I’m working on a game of thrones video for
tomorrow.

00:11:01.450 --> 00:11:05.280
My next doctor who video will be saturday
morning before episode 2 airs, and I’ll

00:11:05.280 --> 00:11:12.320
post my review after the episode.

